"to the Slugs. This particular nebula is just that."

#: src-ru/data/events_slug.xml.rawclobber:1186
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"data/events_slug.xml.rawclobber$//textList[@name=\"START_BEACON_SLUG\"]/text[2]"
msgstr ""
"This nebula is home to the telepathic Slugs. They'd sell their own slime for"
" a crate of scrap, but they much prefer to just take it."

#: src-ru/data/events_slug.xml.rawclobber:1187
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"data/events_slug.xml.rawclobber$//textList[@name=\"START_BEACON_SLUG\"]/text[3]"
msgstr ""
"You're told the Slug home world is somewhere in this nebula. You can't see "
"them, but you know they're watching."

#: src-ru/data/events_slug.xml.rawclobber:1188
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"data/events_slug.xml.rawclobber$//textList[@name=\"START_BEACON_SLUG\"]/text[4]"
msgstr ""
"The Slugs that live in this nebula field are a leisure-centered "
"civilization. Everything in Slug life is done in the pursuit of more "
"currency and more time in which to spend it on extravagant ventures. This, "
"inevitably, leads to much treachery in open space."

#: src-ru/data/events_slug.xml.rawclobber:1189
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"data/events_slug.xml.rawclobber$//textList[@name=\"START_BEACON_SLUG\"]/text[5]"
msgstr ""
"The Slugs developed on an ocean planet where the ability to telepathically "
"sense another organism was more important than sight. Today they use this "
"ability to navigate unfettered the depths of the nebulas they inhabit."

#: src-ru/data/events_slug.xml.rawclobber:1190
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"data/events_slug.xml.rawclobber$//textList[@name=\"START_BEACON_SLUG\"]/text[6]"
msgstr ""
"You've arrived in a Slug nebula. These harmful telepathic creatures are "
"cunning and selfish to the core. When flying here, remember only one thing: "
"they already know of your presence here. Be extremely careful."

#: src-ru/data/events_slug.xml.rawclobber:1191
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"data/events_slug.xml.rawclobber$//textList[@name=\"START_BEACON_SLUG\"]/text[7]"
msgstr ""
"Immediately upon arrival in the sector, you notice a fine weapon in perfect "
"condition right at the side of the ship. The eyes of your crewmembers shine "
"with joy, and the pilot takes out a bottle of Zoltan grog. However, upon "
"turning the scanners on, you see it's only an asteroid. Is this another "
"hypnotic trick of the sly Slugs?.."

#: src-ru/data/events_slug.xml.rawclobber:1192
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"data/events_slug.xml.rawclobber$//textList[@name=\"START_BEACON_SLUG\"]/text[8]"
msgstr ""
"Nebulae have always been pretty dangerous places. The settlement of such "
"sector by Slugs, ideally suited to such conditions, makes them an extremely "
"unfavorable place..."

#: src-ru/data/events_slug.xml.rawclobber:1193
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"data/events_slug.xml.rawclobber$//textList[@name=\"START_BEACON_SLUG\"]/text[9]"
msgstr "The inscription on the beacon reads: \"We know.\" Damn telepathic Slugs!"

#: src-ru/data/events_slug.xml.rawclobber:1194
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"data/events_slug.xml.rawclobber$//textList[@name=\"START_BEACON_SLUG\"]/text[10]"
msgstr ""
"This sector is controlled by Slugs. These creatures are willing to do "
"anything just to get precious scrap, so be on the alert!"

#: src-ru/data/events_slug.xml.rawclobber:1195
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"data/events_slug.xml.rawclobber$//textList[@name=\"START_BEACON_SLUG\"]/text[11]"
msgstr ""
"This nebula is controlled by Slugs. It's worth knowing two things about this"
" race: the first — Slugs lie just as readily as they breathe; and the second"
" — they'll do anything and everything they can to take possession of your "
"scrap, including open robbery."

#: src-ru/data/events_slug.xml.rawclobber:1196
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"data/events_slug.xml.rawclobber$//textList[@name=\"START_BEACON_SLUG\"]/text[12]"
msgstr ""
"An ancient legend says that there are Slugs that speak the truth... But the "
"chance to find a living unicorn or Pegasus is much higher."

#: src-ru/data/events_slug.xml.rawclobber:1197
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"data/events_slug.xml.rawclobber$//textList[@name=\"START_BEACON_SLUG\"]/text[13]"
msgstr ""
"This nebula is infamous not so much for its storms, which make electronics "
"go haywire, as by the Slugs inhabiting it. Actually, it can also be "
"considered the second reason, as to why ships disappear here."

#: src-ru/data/events_slug.xml.rawclobber:1198
